WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.528
(audience cheering)
- She was featured

00:00:01.528 --> 00:00:04.500
on this month's cover of Health magazine.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.500
And it's the first un-retouched cover

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.829
in the magazine's history.

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:08.662
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:09.495
So let's talk about your cover.

00:00:09.495 --> 00:00:11.040
I mean, is it hard?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.640
Because everything nowadays is
so filtered and so retouched.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.650
Was it hard and scary,

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.290
especially six months
after you're having a baby?

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.220
- Oh, it was so scary.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.053
And leading up,

00:00:19.053 --> 00:00:21.310
I was still breast feeding
when I did this shoot.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.010
And I was just freaking
out the whole time--

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:24.843
- That part was probably good

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:25.900
because they're real full (laughs)

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.811
- I didn't need the help.

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:29.783
- Oh, some of us do, Kate.

00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.520
(audience laughs)

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.200
- I didn't need any extra.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.580
No.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.520
But you know, un-retouched is actually

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.608
really hard for everybody
on set, I noticed.

00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:41.530
The makeup artist and the hair stylist,

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.767
everyone's like, "Oh my God!

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.097
"What are we gonna do with
her bruise on her knee?

00:00:45.097 --> 00:00:46.337
"Who's gonna cover it?

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:47.640
"The makeup's not covering it!"

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.270
Everything's very stressful.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.060
And doing it in natural lighting

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.840
adds that very real element as well.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.734
- Boy, natural lighting is not my friend.

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.501
(audience laughs)

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.003
- That's such a lie.
- I like a soft,

00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:00.552
amber dim light.
- Stop!

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.070
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.550
No, but it was really
important for me to do this.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.370
Because we're on Instagram all the time,

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.770
and we see people
Photoshopping everything.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.430
You're like, when does it end?

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.214
And when you're scrolling on Instagram,

00:01:13.214 --> 00:01:16.540
you constantly compare
yourself to these other people.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.010
And for me, I wanted to take a step back

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.380
and show a real moment

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.140
of someone who actually
is six months postpartum,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.322
is not being Photoshopped.

00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:27.380
And be that real person and real influence

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.213
for other people.
- I love it.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.380
(audience applauds)
I think it's awesome.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.220
We have four kids,

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.900
and two of them are teenagers.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.733
One's almost a teenager.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:36.900
And literally it's so hard on social media

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.450
because everybody compares you.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.506
And if you don't get enough likes,

00:01:39.506 --> 00:01:40.810
it cancels something out.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.260
It's like everything has to
be validated in social media,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.540
and everything is filtered,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.373
so I think it's really cool

00:01:45.373 --> 00:01:46.206
that you're such a,

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.039
I mean, you're a super model.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.110
So all these girls look up to you.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:48.990
Especially like,

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.570
it's really cool that you're
brave and okay to do it.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.360
- Yeah, and why are we
comparing our bodies post partum

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.520
to all these Photoshopped?

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.770
When we should be admiring our bodies

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.148
that we even created life!

00:01:58.148 --> 00:02:00.329
- Creating humans.
- Conversation should change!

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:02.090
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.159
- Like, created central nervous systems.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:05.720
- Exactly!
- You're welcome.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:08.330
- Give ourselves a little
bit more time to bounce back.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.360
We don't need to do it two months.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.030
- I'm in the middle of bouncing.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.740
(audience and Kate laughs)

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.265
No, but even before the
Health magazine cover though,

00:02:17.265 --> 00:02:18.610
people always used to say

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:19.900
that you're too curvy.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.733
Which I'm like,

00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:23.297
"I wish I was Kate Upton, the super curvy

00:02:23.297 --> 00:02:24.410
"super model."

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.810
Is that nuts to you?

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:26.980
- When it was first happening,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.480
obviously it was really hard,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.313
'cause I was like,

00:02:29.313 --> 00:02:30.217
"I work out all the time.

00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:32.300
"Why is everyone calling me fat?"

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.330
And now the conversation
has completely changed

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.163
and people are like,

00:02:35.163 --> 00:02:36.940
"What? When did people say that?"

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.880
And that just shows how
the industry's changing,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.160
how our voice matters,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.530
and things can change.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.923
We mean something.
(audience applauds)

00:02:42.923 --> 00:02:43.990
We can change something.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.820
- Have you connected with other women

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.120
because of this cover?

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:47.953
- Yes!

00:02:47.953 --> 00:02:48.786
You know, because of this cover

00:02:48.786 --> 00:02:50.822
I actually started a hashtag,

00:02:50.822 --> 00:02:52.480
#sharestrong

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.770
just on Instagram

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.010
to create a community

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:55.971
where we could all share

00:02:55.971 --> 00:02:57.350
our real selves,

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.240
or what continues to motivate us

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.870
to continue being strong.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.040
And a lot of people are
posting no makeup selfies,

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.220
or their stories.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.050
It's so great to go on that hashtag

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.500
and get inspiration from
all these other women.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.700
Because we're so strong.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.640
And to be able to share
in each other's strength

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.634
is what makes women so amazing.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:15.702
- Absolutely.

00:03:15.702 --> 00:03:18.203
(audience applauds)
And also, it's,

00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:19.552
people don't realize

00:03:19.552 --> 00:03:21.330
even if you're a woman
and you've never had kids,

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.800
there's so much going on
after you have a baby.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.170
Not only your body is just giving up,

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.320
but your emotional state is kinda crazy.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.880
So somebody talking to someone

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.330
that's just had a baby in a photo shoot

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.740
saying, "You need to loosen,"

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:36.090
that will send you in a spiral.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:36.923
- Oh yeah.

00:03:36.923 --> 00:03:37.850
The hormones are crazy.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.240
And no one talks about it.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.730
The hormones after pregnancy, for me,

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.150
were crazier than when I was pregnant.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.952
And it took forever for them to calm down.

00:03:46.952 --> 00:03:49.040
Months after breast feeding.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.080
I might still be hormonal.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:51.913
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:51.913 --> 00:03:53.090
- No, here's my best,

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.330
this is my best story.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.163
So I was,

00:03:55.163 --> 00:03:55.996
I freaked out.

00:03:55.996 --> 00:03:56.829
'cause I had to,

00:03:56.829 --> 00:03:57.662
I was pumping because I was
working at the same time--

00:03:57.662 --> 00:03:59.020
- Which is the worst!

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.570
- Pumping is the worst!
- The worst!

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.630
- It's so painful,

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.210
I don't care what anyone says.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.043
Anyway,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.880
but somebody had kinda tossed out,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.710
and it was only a tiny bit of breast milk

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:08.780
left in the bottle.
- No.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:09.613
No!

00:04:09.613 --> 00:04:11.500
- I lost my ever living,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.590
like a crazy person.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.880
Went in my closet and just (cries)

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.210
collapsed on the floor and was crying.

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.043
'cause I was like,

00:04:17.043 --> 00:04:19.103
"You have no idea how
hard I worked for that!"

00:04:19.103 --> 00:04:19.960
(audience laughs)

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.130
And really, there was like
nothing in the bottle.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:22.963
I'm crazy.

00:04:22.963 --> 00:04:24.680
But literally, it's just a hormonal period

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.270
and I don't think people
take that into account,

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.870
especially when we're
women in the public eye.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.850
Like, it is a hard time.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.190
- And our energy is literally
being sucked out of us

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.982
so you don't feel like yourself.

00:04:34.982 --> 00:04:37.161
- Literally, it's being sucked out of us.

00:04:37.161 --> 00:04:38.610
- Literally, it's being sucked out of you.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.360
It is so difficult.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.977
And something people
need to talk about more.

00:04:42.977 --> 00:04:44.460
- I 100%,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.168
I talk about it any chance I can.

00:04:46.168 --> 00:04:47.001
(audience laughs)

00:04:47.001 --> 00:04:50.000
I complain about pregnancy
and all that any chance I can.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.830
It's beautiful, and I love my children,

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:52.663
and you love your child.
- Yes.

00:04:52.663 --> 00:04:53.496
- But here's my thing.

00:04:53.496 --> 00:04:54.979
Your share strong is your daughter, right?

00:04:54.979 --> 00:04:55.812
- Yes.

00:04:55.812 --> 00:04:56.840
- So how is she your share strong?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:57.673
I love that.

00:04:57.673 --> 00:04:59.440
- Well you know, I want to

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.300
be the example she can look up to.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.370
And I want to create
a happy, healthy world

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.140
for her to grow up in.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.300
- Yeah, of course.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.860
We actually have a mom here today

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.180
who was inspired by Kate.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.554
Say hello to Alex.

00:05:11.554 --> 00:05:14.290
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.270
You look beautiful.
- [Kate] Beautiful.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.140
- Like, the red lip with the red skirt,

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.550
I'm into it.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:20.910
So what do you want to say to Kate?

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.100
- I'm Alex, I'm a new mom,

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.030
and I just want to say thank you.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.090
When I was pregnant,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.504
I was a little over,

00:05:26.504 --> 00:05:27.930
I mean before I was pregnant,

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.360
I was a little over 100 pounds,

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.080
and I'm ashamed to admit it,

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.290
but I was so afraid to gain weight

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.090
and what I would look like.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.540
And then I got pregnant,

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.050
and I found out I was having a baby girl.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.720
And I knew that if

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.100
I wanted her to love herself

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.930
that it had to start with me.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.410
I loved being pregnant,

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.410
I loved the big belly.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.580
But then towards the end

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.700
I started getting those
nervous feelings again.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.440
Like, what am I gonna look like?

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:54.570
Will I still be strong?

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.930
What will people think?

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.600
And I had her, and I loved my body.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.210
But then I saw you on the cover of Health,

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.170
and un-retouched

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.370
and it was so inspiring.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.990
It made me realize like,

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:12.862
I don't owe anybody pretty
or perfect or skinny.

00:06:12.862 --> 00:06:15.270
(audience applauds and cheers)
Or anything.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.440
And to just

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.290
be an example

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.180
for my daughter

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.980
and to just be someone she can look up to

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.000
and be strong for my daughter

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.570
is the best thing that I could be.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.610
And you don't know how
many people you've touched,

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.580
so just thank you so much.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.530
- Thank you.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.920
We're all on our own journeys,

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.550
it's so important for us to share them.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:32.912
Thank you so much.

00:06:32.912 --> 00:06:33.745
- Thank you.

00:06:33.745 --> 00:06:34.578
- I mean, what do you think about that?

00:06:34.578 --> 00:06:36.480
There's got to be so many women,

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.840
especially in the field that you're in,

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.210
that you touch like that.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.223
- No, it means so much to me,

00:06:40.223 --> 00:06:42.220
because you know,

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.580
when you hear all the criticism

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.413
sometimes you're like,

00:06:44.413 --> 00:06:45.840
"Why am I doing this?"

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.490
And stories like that I realize,

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.040
this is exactly why I'm doing this

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.570
and we're all in it together.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:52.140
And we're all experiencing it together.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.814
So thank you so much for sharing that.

00:06:53.814 --> 00:06:54.647
(audience applauds)

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.370
- And beauty is many things.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:57.454
My favorite thing is,

00:06:57.454 --> 00:06:59.500
why I think you're so
beautiful coming out,

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.540
yes aesthetically you're beautiful,

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.030
but you have a certain
confidence about you.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:02.863
And I love,

00:07:02.863 --> 00:07:04.600
I think confidence is so sexy.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.490
It's the sexiest thing
on a man or a woman.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.323
I think

00:07:07.323 --> 00:07:08.620
just be happy, be confident,

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.830
and you'll exude it.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.500
- Yeah, but we all go
through our ups and downs.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.530
We don't all feel confident all the time.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.592
But it's working,

00:07:14.592 --> 00:07:17.550
getting back to that confident
place, that's so important.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.530
And that journey there.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.937
- Yes, I love you!

